<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on June 10.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on June 10.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Hanbonn Brother     SLD June 03     12,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>Blaji Diplomat	SLD June 07     33,600	Dubai</p>
<p>Bihor		   SLD June 04	5,000	Mozambique</p>
<p>Hantinh 06	    SLD June 02	1,200	China</p>
<p>Great Concert	 SLD June 03     12,600	Indonesia</p>
<p>Olga		    SLD June 06     12,000	South Korea</p>
<p>Jiao Cheng	    SLD June 02     14,000	China</p>
<p>Dai Hong Dan	  SLD June 03	8,000	China</p>
<p>Kapitan Bakanov     SLD June 08     11,400	South Korea</p>
<p>Chahaya Sejati	SLD June 06	1,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Nan Ping Shan	 ETD June 09     14,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>Huang Hua	     ETD June 11     13,850	Japan</p>
<p>Long Chan Jiang     ETD June 11     13,500	China</p>
<p>Jilin		   ETD June 10	9,500	South Korea</p>
<p>Princess of Lorne   ETD June 14     13,200	Tanzania</p>
<p>Lucnum		  N/A		  9,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Hua Tian		ETD June 09     14,000	South Korea</p>
<p>Solar Glory	   ETD June 17     13,500	China</p>
<p>Phu Yen		 ETA June 10	2,000	China</p>
<p>Surin Navee	   ETA June 10	8,000	Japan</p>
<p>Sun Vazs		ETR June 10     13,300	South Korea</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	   ETR June 16     14,000	Japan</p>
<p>Jutha Buddharaksa   ETR June 13     12,000	Japan</p>
<p>Orient Express	ETA June 11	1,200	Cambodia</p>
<p>Galactica	     ETA June 13     15,750	Malaysia</p>
<p>Pipob Samut	   ETA June 15     18,000	Japan</p>
<p>Evpo Ageos	    ETA June 10     13,300	South Korea</p>
<p>Ivan Syrykh	   ETA June 13-14  10,500	South Korea</p>
<p>Alam Teguh	    ETA June 13     16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Won San		 ETA June 15     14,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>An Lu Jiang	   N/A		 14,000	China</p>
<p>Al Qua Mar	    L/CAN 12-18     14,000	Iran</p>
<p>Orient Express I    L/CAN 23-26	1,200	Cambodia</p>
<p>Delight		 ETA June 20	N/A	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Sangthai Quartz     ETR June 13	500	  Singapore</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
